<p>As the widening U.S.-Israeli military campaign in Iran moves beyond its opening strikes, President Donald Trump said the operation could last weeks — and could run longer. He framed the strikes as necessary to eliminate what he called an Iranian threat. He also refused to rule out deploying U.S. ground troops “if necessary”. The conflict is also spilling across the region. Reporting describes exchanges involving Israel and says attacks have spread into Gulf countries and Lebanon. Several outlets have also reported heavy casualties in Iran since the strikes began. Even with the grim toll, governments appear to be looking for ways to keep the fighting from widening further. Reporting says Gulf states have urged allies to press Washington toward a diplomatic off-ramp after Iranian reprisals.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/tHyqWOEYA7iKF9BFpC8HoT8IuHccmMhCDfyUCmv6nG1nfRtXncIZ39_RAJXXP-rJW4e82juODEMM7VdeVoslPGlFG4rShSkMqCveXUGs5AkP93Up4E1obgPa-2FTCHTj_hL-xtRfG2Ecz3e7Rst-7LMipIam405q8jSJU1IvozL192sOTdNxFgTDB5N2XRdRZyn9rfoQv8nYPOFmwC4ibCVeag5n3KMD' alt='People gather belongings from damaged homes in Tehran after U.S.-Israeli airstrikes, as President Trump signals more strikes ahead.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>U.S. losses: El País reported Washington confirmed a fourth U.S. service member had been killed and said three F-15 fighter jets were downed by “friendly fire” in Kuwait.</li><li>U.S. military posture: Dawn reported a top U.S. general said the U.S. had air superiority over Iran and warned more losses should be expected.</li><li>Iran claims: Dawn reported Iranian officials said the country was prepared for a long war and claimed it had hit more than 500 targets.</li><li>Domestic pressure: Semafor cited polling showing most Americans disapprove of the strikes and noted rising gas prices as a potential pressure point for the White House.</li><li>Weapons posture: NDTV reported Trump said the U.S. has a “virtually unlimited” supply of weapons to fight wars “forever” and “successfully”.</li></ul><blockquote>We projected for four to five weeks, but we have the capability to go longer than that - Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio: Rubio warned that “the hardest hits are yet to come,” the South China Morning Post reported. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/us/article/3345185/iran-strikes-day-3-trump-says-iran-operation-will-continue-5-weeks'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Iran (Ali Larijani): Larijani said Tehran “will not negotiate with the United States,” according to El País. (<a href='https://english.elpais.com/international/2026-03-02/iranian-regime-says-it-will-not-negotiate-with-the-united-states.html'>El País</a>)</li><li>U.S. Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth: Hegseth said it would be “foolishness” to expect U.S. officials to publicly specify “here’s exactly how far we’ll go,” and declined to spell out limits on U.S. actions. (<a href='https://time.com/7382186/iran-ground-troops-trump/'>Time</a>)</li><li>France (Le Monde): Le Monde reported Trump suggested the U.S. could retaliate “soon” after two suspected Iranian drones struck the U.S. embassy in Riyadh. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/02/trump-does-not-rule-out-sending-us-troops-to-iran_6751016_4.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/us/article/3345185/iran-strikes-day-3-trump-says-iran-operation-will-continue-5-weeks'>Trump says Iran war could last a month or longer as conflict widens</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-iran-war-white-house/'>Trump says strikes were &quot;last best chance&quot; to take out Iran threat</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://time.com/7382186/iran-ground-troops-trump/'>Trump Says He Would Deploy Ground Troops to Iran “If Necessary”</a> - time.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/i-dont-get-bored-trump-says-us-can-sustain-iran-war